thread:
Maya Chen: Heads-up on a UX regression in the Console at narrow widths (<360px). The top action bar wraps and pushes the table down, creating a second horizontal scrollbar on Safari iOS. Screenshot: https://staging.redwood.internal/ux/bug-425.png

Priya Singh: Seen this on smaller Android devices too. Primary action buttons (Run, Export, Retry) wrap below the search field. That makes the hit targets tiny and causes accidental taps.

Jonah Kim: Repro on iPhone 8 simulator. CSS flex-wrap is the culprit. We had compact controls to save space, but they still overflow when labels are visible.

Ezra Blake: Quick proposals: (1) collapse to icon-only buttons at <= 360px, (2) move secondary actions into an overflow menu, or (3) use a stacked layout where the action bar becomes a single-row sticky toolbar with horizontal scrolling but larger tap targets. I'm leaning to (1) + overflow menu.

Maya Chen: +1 for icon-only with tooltip on long-press for mobile. But we must keep affordance for new users 12; maybe add a brief one-time hint 'Tap icons for actions' on first visit.

Priya Singh: Accessibility: if we collapse to icons, add aria-label and visible focus ring. Also ensure the overflow menu items are reachable by keyboard and TalkBack.

Jonah Kim: For the table scrollbar: Safari on iOS shows a second horizontal scroll when the table width and container width mismatch due to the wrapped bar. A simpler fix is to make the top bar position: sticky and not contribute to layout when it wraps.

Ezra Blake: CSS POC:
```css
.top-actions {
  display: flex;
  gap: 8px;
  flex-wrap: nowrap;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.top-actions .action {
  min-width: 44px; /* mobile tap target */
}
@media (max-width: 360px) {
  .top-actions {
    justify-content: flex-end;
  }
  .action-label { display: none; }
  .action-icon { display: inline-block; }
}
```
This hides labels and keeps tap targets consistent. Will test.

Priya Singh: Please include a visible fallback for screen readers: add aria-expanded on the overflow button and aria-controls linking to the menu.

Jonah Kim: UX question: should Copy / Export be primary? Analytics show Copy is used 4x more. Maybe we demote Export to the overflow and keep Copy as a primary icon.

Maya Chen: Good catch. Make Copy the prominent icon. Rename Export -> More actions. Update copy in the tooltip: 'Copy ID' and 'Export CSV' in the menu.

QA-Bot: Running narrow-width visual tests on: iPhone SE (320px), Android Small (360px), Safari iOS 15, Chrome Android 12. Results will post here when done.

Ezra Blake: I'll land a small change on feature/compact-actions and include visual diffs for 320 and 360 widths. Also adding unit test to assert .action label is hidden at <=360px.

Maya Chen: Assigning to @Ezra for implementation, @Priya for a11y review, and @Jonah for visual sign-off. If all green, ship to canary tomorrow. Thanks!
